-- title:
--   Postprocess Sandwich By Outer Prod Snd Outcome
-- statement:
--   **Second-coordinate postprocessing of a sandwiched product.**
--
--   Let $A$ and $B$ be finite submeasurements with outcome types $\alpha$ and $\beta$, and fix $b\in\beta$. Postprocess the sandwiched submeasurement with outcome $(a,b')$ and effect $A_aB_{b'}A_a$ by its second projection. The resulting effect is
--
--   $$
--   \left(\operatorname{postprocess}\left(\operatorname{sandwichByOuterSubMeas}(A,B),\operatorname{Prod.snd}\right)\right)_b=\sum_{a\in\alpha}A_aB_bA_a.
--   $$
--
--   This finite-fiber identity exposes the averaged sandwich used by `gCommStabilityR` and identifies the phase-two question defect with the scalar stability defect.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.postprocess_sandwichByOuter_prod_snd_outcome`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
